  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public int[][] combinationSum(int[] candidates, int target) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return new int[0][];\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "To avoid counting [2,3] and [3,2] separately, only ever add values in non-decreasing order.",
    "Sort, then backtrack from a start index: you may reuse the current value or move to a later one.",
    "sort candidates\ndef build(start, remaining, path):\n    if remaining == 0: record path\n    for i in start..n-1:\n        if candidates[i] > remaining: break\n        build(i, remaining - candidates[i], path + [candidates[i]])",
    "Passing `i` (not `i + 1`) allows reuse; breaking early on a too-large value prunes the search. Output is exponential in the worst case."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(answer size)",
    "space": "O(target)"
  },
